## T-371: Debug fade_rect + Golden Test

### Root Cause
`LinearInterp.interpTypeCode()` returned 0 — which the Rive spec defines as "hold".
`gen_animation.go` suppresses emission when `InterpolationType==0` (hold is default).
Result: keyframes silently treated as hold → opacity stayed at 0.0 → 0 pixels rendered.

### Fix
Swapped interpTypeCode values: LinearInterp=1, HoldInterp=0 (matches Rive spec).
This also corrects color_cycle.riv which was discretely jumping instead of interpolating.

### New Examples
- `fade_rect.riv`: color-alpha approach (KeyFrameColor on SolidColor.colorValue, alpha 0→255→0)
  matching official Rive editor export structure
- `fade_rect_opacity.riv`: shape opacity approach (KeyFrameDouble on PropOpacity), now works
  after interpTypeCode fix

### Tests: all pass (go test ./... clean)

