[T-373] PROJ_RIVE-GO_CODE_FIX_VISUAL_BUGS — 2026-05-08

Bug 1 — color_cycle loop snap
Root cause: forward Loop mode with a duplicate endpoint keyframe at frame 90 means the
runtime plays [0, 90), reaching ~97% red at frame 89.999 before snapping to exact red at
frame 0. Even though the snap is red→red (tiny delta), it was perceptible.
Fix: changed to PingPong loop (LoopType=2), removed duplicate endpoint keyframe (frame 90),
reduced duration to 60. Animation now goes red→blue→green→blue→red… with smooth reversal.

Bug 2 — gradient_ellipse flat circle (no visible gradient)
Root cause: FillGradient coordinates (50, 200, 350, 200) were in artboard space. The Rive
web runtime interprets LinearGradient start/end in shape-local space (origin at shape
center). With the shape centered at (200,200), the artboard coords were (−150,0)→(150,0)
relative to shape — which happened to span the ellipse, but the y-value 200 was 200 units
below the shape center in local space, placing the gradient axis far outside the shape and
producing a near-uniform color.
Fix: changed to shape-local coords (-75, 0, 75, 0) — horizontal gradient spanning the
ellipse radius (±75) in local space.

All tests pass (go test ./...). Files regenerated, preview page descriptions updated.

